{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he said, \"Tomorrow.\"</b> Rav Shmuel ben Hofni said: It is not the way of a person to ask except that the plague be removed from him immediately. But Pharaoh thought that the configuration of the celestial stars had brought the frogs upon Egypt, and that Moses knew this, and Pharaoh reckoned that now the time for the removal of the frogs had arrived. Therefore he tested him by delaying, and said, \"Tomorrow.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:35.637747115Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}